  "body": "**Stacked on #395** (lathe holder bodies), which is on #381. The #396 work is 679380d5.\n\n## What changed\n- **The zone.** A lathe body can carry an optional **insert zone**: a box in the turning tool frame around the tip, `InsertZone { lo, hi }`, in `BodyFrame::Lathe`.\n- **Exclusion.** Each facet is clipped against the outer side of each of the box's six faces. Only what lies strictly inside the box leaves the clearance bands; every part outside it is still banded exactly.\n  - The size, flatness and degeneracy checks still read the whole mesh.\n  - Display and placement are untouched.\n  - The stamp moves because the bands move.\n- **The bound, so a zone can't hide the holder.** No tool field states the insert's size, so the cap is the steel the insert sits on:\n  - the box must be finite and must hold the tip;\n  - from the tip it may reach no farther than the tool's `diameter` along each axis;\n  - for groove and form blades, at most `width/2` along the spindle;\n  - every cap is held to 25.4 mm, the largest ISO turning insert's inscribed circle;\n  - some of the body must stay outside the box.\n  - Refusals are by name, at command creation, `ChangeTool` and load.\n  - Limitation: inside that cap the zone excuses what it holds. Holder steel beyond the box is judged as before, and the shoulder-rub test pins that. See `docs/decisions/396-lathe-insert-zone.md`.\n- **Command.** `LatheBodySpec.zone`, and `SetToolBody::insert_zone(world, tool, Option<InsertZone>)` sets or clears the zone and keeps the mesh. Same command, so undo and redo come free.\n- **Project file: no new version.**\n  - The zone is an optional `insert_zone` key, left out when there is none, so the bytes are unchanged without one.\n  - A reader older than #396 skips the key and judges the whole body. That over-reports and blocks the post; it never passes a rub.\n\n## How tested\n- New `crates/app/tests/turning_insert_zone.rs` (5 tests):\n  - a plate-plus-shank mesh on a plain OD finish is a `HolderHit` today, and posts clean with the zone set (undo and redo included);\n  - in a bar, rough then finish, the plate's own chip is cleared by the zone;\n  - **a real shoulder rub is still convicted with the zone set** (3.2 mm short, post refused);\n  - refusals by name: no lathe body, zones past the cap (z 20, z −30, a grooving blade's ±1.5 against its 1.0 cap), a NaN corner, a zone missing the tip, a body wholly inside its zone, and a `ChangeTool` to a smaller body;\n  - save → load → save is byte-identical, and an over-cap zone in a file refuses the load.\n- `crates/tools` unit tests: 3 new; all 24 pass, including a randomized check that every facet point outside the zone stays within its band's radii.\n- `turning_holder` still passes 8/8.\n- `scripts/gate.sh quick` against #395's branch is green except #415 (red on main). `clippy -p camcraft-tools -p camcraft-app --tests -D warnings` is clean.\n\n## Not exercised\n- No GUI for the zone yet: it's set through the command and the project file. The editor's lathe-body UI would follow #399.\n\nChangelog: A lathe holder body can carry an insert zone, so a vendor mesh that includes its insert plate no longer reads the plate's own chip as a holder rub; zones larger than one of the tool's inserts are refused by name (#396)\n\nFixes #396\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
